      "heading": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test",
      "content": {
        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Who should choose a child's career is best answered as a shared process in which the child owns the decision, parents provide information, resources and perspective, and both agree on trials and review points, because forced choices often lead to disengagement and later regret."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Let the child lead with their interests and strengths, add the family's constraints and facts, run a small trial and agree a review date."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Nothing here is psychological advice."
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "proof",
      "title": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test"
